how long a stalled backup stays SILENT is the 'daemon signal after Ns' figure
in each phase above, read next to the daemon's own declared backoff.
litestream backs off exponentially on consecutive errors, so that number
GROWS with each successive failure, and it is measured against a wait bound
of 70s -- which is what makes a surface count as invisible.
A surface that is silent for 30 s and one that is silent forever are
different findings, and only the second is a reason to distrust the daemon
log as an alerting source.

